                <pb facs="0742" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/447: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-10-15T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                                1917, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your October 2, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>Your understanding as to suspension of indemnity payments is correct. If other
                    co-belligerent governments agree to proposed international tariff commission
                    this Government will appoint Commissioners with the understanding that the
                    revised tariff before it could become effective should presumably be
                    incorporated into a new treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
